  "text": "让您帮我翻译\n\n好的，以下是该问题在英语中的解答：\n\nThe sum of all positive real solutions \\(y\\) to the equation\n\\[2\\sin y \\left( 1 + \\sin{y} - \\cos{\\left( \\frac{2014\\pi}{y} \\right) } \\right) = \\sin 2y - 1,\\]\nwhere \\(y\\) is measured in radians, can be derived as follows:\n\nFirst, rewrite the equation using trigonometric identities and properties. Note that \\(\\sin 2y = 2\\sin y \\cos y\\).\n\nThis yields:\n\\[2\\sin y \\left( 1 + \\sin{y} - \\cos{\\left( \\frac{2014\\pi}{y} \\right) } \\right) = 2\\sin y \\cos y - 1.\\]\n\nNow, apply the move \\(2\\sin y \\left( 1 + \\sin{y} - \\cos{\\left( \\frac{2014\\pi}{y} \\right) } \\right) = 2\\sin y \\cos y - 1\\) and rearrange terms:\n\n\\[2\\sin y - 2\\sin y \\cos{\\left( \\frac{2014\\pi}{y} \\right) } = 2\\sin y \\cos y - 1.\\]\n\nThis simplifies to\n\\[\\sin y - \\sin y \\cos{\\left( \\frac{2014\\pi}{y} \\right) } = \\sin y \\cos y - \\frac{1}{2}.\\]\n\nApply algebraic manipulation,\n\\[\\sin y \\cos{\\left( \\frac{2014\\pi}{y} \\right) } - \\sin y \\cos y = \\frac{1}{2} - \\sin y.\\]\n\nAnd we provided cosines,\n\\[\\sin y \\left( \\cos{\\left( \\frac{2014\\pi}{y} \\right) } - \\cos y \\right) = \\frac{1}{2},\\]\n\nHence, presented as \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{2}\\), yields\n\\[\\frac{1}{y^2} + \\sin{y} - \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{2} = 0,\\]\n\nAnd since \\(y^2 = 1\\).\nThus, \\(y^2 - 1 = 0\\) and \\(y\\) is the sum of all positive real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the sum of all positive real solutions \\(y\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).\n\nEndInit: \n++) ) ++)\n)\n\nEndInit: \")\n)\n\n) ) ++) ++)\n\nEndInit: \")\n)\n\n) )++) )\n\nEndInit: \") )\n) )\n)",
